# A page's fonts are fetched when its text needs them, not when its sheets
# declare them. fonts-on-demand.html declares six and opens with text in
# one: one is asked for. Each step then brings the first need of another —
# bold words, Greek letters (a font kept to their range), a width in the
# `ch` of the font of a box with no text in it, and a canvas's text, asked
# for through document.fonts.load() — and the font nothing uses is never
# asked for. The counts are of the fonts asked for since the script began.
resize 800 600
open fonts-on-demand.html
assert-title fonts
assert-fonts-asked 1
advance 100
assert-title bold
assert-fonts-asked 2
advance 100
assert-title greek
assert-fonts-asked 3
advance 100
assert-title sized 100
assert-fonts-asked 4
advance 100
assert-title drawn
assert-fonts-asked 5
